      "from": "conversations",
      "to": "knowledge_gaps",
      "fromCardinality": "one",
      "toCardinality": "many",
      "fromOptional": true,
      "toOptional": true
    }
  ],
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read it",
      "items": [
        "Each box is a table with every column, in the order the migrations add them",
        "PK = primary key · FK = points to another table · UK = must be unique",
        "Lines show the main links; a crow's foot means \"many\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Not drawn, to keep it readable",
      "items": [
        "created_by, resolved_by, reviewed_by, taken_over_by, author_id, reported_by and actor_id all point to profiles",
        "staff.profile_id → profiles (team login) · login_codes.profile_id → profiles · conversations.profile_id → profiles",
        "agent_runs, agent_traces and assistant_reports → conversations · contact_changes, escalations, notifications → patients",
        "waitlist.staff_id → staff · waitlist and patient_memories.conversation_id → conversations"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Rules the database enforces",
      "items": [
        "No double bookings: exclusion constraints on appointments (per doctor and per patient)",
        "Unique pairs: login_codes (purpose, email), contact_changes (patient_id, field), knowledge_docs (group_key, language), knowledge_chunks (doc_id, chunk_index)",
        "A patient profile holds no email or phone: those live on patients",
        "team emails are unique (partial index on profiles where role ≠ patient)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What changed since the first design",
      "items": [
        "Supabase Auth is gone: profiles no longer link to auth.users",
        "Sign-in moved into the backend: auth_sessions and login_codes",
        "Only the service role can read or write any table",
        "patients.intake is a JSON object keyed by intake_fields.key"
      ]
    }
  ]
